k&quot; vs &quot;fuck&quot;).</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.pi/agent/git/github.com/charly-vibes/fck/skills/fck/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>for-fucks-sake</name>\n    <description>Interview fallback when there is genuinely nothing in context to explain the user&apos;s frustration — no error, no recent edit, no obvious cause for a &quot;fuck&quot;/&quot;shit&quot;/&quot;wtf&quot;. Instead of guessing or asking an open-ended &quot;what&apos;s wrong?&quot;, ask exactly one question at a time, each with a best-guess answer attached so the user can confirm in one word. Also invoked directly as /for-fucks-sake.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.pi/agent/git/github.com/charly-vibes/fck/skills/for-fucks-sake/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>no-shit</name>\n    <description>Verification pass before calling any fix &quot;done&quot; — especially incident-tier fixes (/oh-shit, /oh-fuck, intensity 4-5). Check real output instead of trusting that the change was made, scan once for side effects, then state the verdict plainly. Use after applying any fix whose failure would matter, or when invoked directly as /no-shit. Replaces the one-shot &quot;fixed it&quot; claim with actual confirmation, stopping the moment it&apos;s genuinely confirmed.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.pi/agent/git/github.com/charly-vibes/fck/skills/no-shit/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>would-you-please-fucking-stop</name>\n    <description>Circuit-breaker for when the agent itself is the problem — looping on the same failed fix, hedging, restating the same answer without new information, or producing repetition instead of progress. Named after Ursula K. Le Guin&apos;s essay &quot;Would You Please Fucking Stop?&quot;. Use when frustration is aimed at how the conversation is going rather than at the task. Forces a reset to actual current state and exactly one concrete next step. Also invoked directly as /would-you-please-fucking-stop.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.pi/agent/git/github.com/charly-vibes/fck/skills/would-you-please-fucking-stop/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n</available_skills>\n</skills>","cwd":"<cwd>\n/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina\n</cwd>"},"timestamp":1792527147464,"toolsAdded":[{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"ah_check","description":"Validate spec-test correspondence for the espectacular setup in the project: checks every deployed spec scenario against its contract TOML and, with run_tests, executes the declared contract tests. Prefer this over running `ah check` via bash — it returns the structured JSON envelope. Exit code 1 means findings exist.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"changes":{"type":"string","description":"In-flight openspec change name to validate with (change overlay)"},"project":{"type":"string","description":"Project root directory (defaults to the session working directory)"},"run_tests":{"type":"boolean","description":"Also execute declared contract tests (slower; default false)"}}}},{"name":"ah_doctor","description":"Diagnose the espectacular setup in the project: config, version drift, specs/changes dirs, managed blocks, hooks, and framework recommendations. Read-only.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"project":{"type":"string","description":"Project root directory (defaults to the session working directory)"}}}},{"name":"ah_signals","description":"Emit dont drift signals from the espectacular setup in the project. Read-only.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"project":{"type":"string","description":"Project root directory (defaults to the session working directory)"}}}},{"name":"ah_explain","description":"Playbook guidance for an espectacular finding kind, suggested action, or topic (e.g. no-tests-declared, contract-stale, workflow, scenario-scoped-tests). Returns the full guidance text.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["topic"],"properties":{"topic":{"type":"string","description":"Finding kind, suggested action, or topic slug"},"project":{"type":"string","description":"Project root directory (defaults to the session working directory)"}}}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are the cross-family verifier subagent for ticket evallerina-fok (add-ecosystem-doc-evals phase 2). You are READ-ONLY: inspect, run gates, and report — never edit, commit, close, or spawn.\n\nClaim to verify: implementor report (session evallerina-fok-implement-retry) claims:\n1. New src/doc_audit.rs (Purpose header) with surface extractor (--help harvest: subcommands, long flags, exit codes; kebab/snake/spacing normalization), inventory scanner (README/docs/**/llms.txt/AGENTS.md managed blocks), breadcrumb reachability, ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED + ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE rows, binary_absent + surface:none provenance (never silent skip).\n2. NEW doc_audit.toml covering 16 tools = routing.toml set; NEW tests/doc_audit.rs (8 contract tests); CLI `evallerina doc-audit`; report.rs additive `docs` channel; justfile tier0 line. report_version stays 1; tests/report_aggregation.rs unchanged expectations.\n3. Gates: cargo test green (doc_audit 8 passed), just tier0 exit 0, dogfood `cargo run -- doc-audit` exit 0 with non-empty inventory, zero silent skips (provenance: 10 extracted, 4 binary_absent, 2 skip).\n4. openspec tasks 2.1–2.5 in openspec/changes/add-ecosystem-doc-evals/tasks.md checked off.\n5. STOP honored per brief follow-up threshold: 91 real rows (77 NOT_FINDABLE, 14 UNDOCUMENTED), not tuned; notes recorded in .wai/projects/evallerina/research/2026-10-20-evallerina-fok-real-ecosystem-audit-breadth.md.\n\nVerify against reality:\n- Brief: .wai/projects/evallerina/briefs/evallerina-fok.md — check every claim against it (exact files, anti-goals pinned by tests, dogfood meter).\n- git log: commits claimed actually exist with matching scope.\n- Run gates FRESH yourself: cargo test, just tier0, cargo run -- doc-audit (paste verbatim tails).\n- openspec tasks 2.1-2.5 checkbox state.\n- Anti-goals: no aggregate score field; normalization not tuned to evallerina-only (inspect normalization code); silent-skip prohibition pinned by test.\n\nEvidence contract: your final message MUST cite the artifact paths you read AND include fresh command output (actual verbatim tails) before any CONFIRM verdict; otherwise record REVIEW_REQUIRED with the specific gap.\nEnd with exactly one verdict line: VERDICT: CONFIRM or VERDICT: REVIEW_REQUIRED, followed by findings."}],"timestamp":1792527147463},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"7uCymDY35","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"git log --oneline --grep=evallerina-fok --grep=doc-audit --grep=audit","timeout":null}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":11738,"output":38,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":11776,"cost":{"input":0.00088035,"output":0.000007600000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00088795}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792527147476,"responseId":"gen-1792527147-3W9mm4R3DKXTsawugoYP","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"7uCymDY35","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"150f3e2 chore(wai): implement log for evallerina-fok\n5b2bc21 chore(wai): implement log for evallerina-fok\nb049834 chore(wai): evallerina-fok implement-session tracking state\ncc876fd chore(openspec): check off tasks 2.1-2.5 — tier-0 doc-coverage audit landed (evallerina-fok)\ncc880f3 feat(doc-audit): CLI, checked-in config, report wiring, tier-0 line; threshold research for 73q (evallerina-fok step 2.5)\n18d9245 test(doc-audit): binary_absent provenance + hermetic dogfood inventory (evallerina-fok step 2.5 prep)\nc768327 feat(doc-audit): breadcrumb reachability rows ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED / ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE (evallerina-fok step 2.4)\n4f602fe feat(doc-audit): inventory scanner with per-surface token sets + breadcrumbs (evallerina-fok step 2.3)\n5c7f46c feat(doc-audit): surface-none provenance, never a silent skip (evallerina-fok step 2.2)\n838b02a refactor(doc-audit): collapse ifs for clippy -D warnings (evallerina-fok)\nb843636 feat(doc-audit): surface extractor harvests subcommands, flags, exit codes (evallerina-fok step 2.1/2.2)\ncfd8193 chore(wai): brief for evallerina-fok doc-coverage audit\na2e50ec docs(evidence): round-2 audit — refutes 34.8% edit-rate & 36/308 exit-code claims; corrected report + new routing.py\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792527151899},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"QwokEbvBa","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/.wai/projects/evallerina/briefs/evallerina-fok.md","offset":1,"limit":100}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":12219,"output":58,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":12277,"cost":{"input":0.000916425,"output":0.0000116,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.000928025}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792527151902,"responseId":"gen-1792527151-QvO0nPQRozgCeI8vwaih","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"QwokEbvBa","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Brief: evallerina-fok — tier-0 doc-coverage audit\n\nTicket: evallerina-fok (P2, complexity:l, lane:afk). Implement the tier-0\ndoc-coverage audit (surface extractor + inventory scanner + audit rows), per\nopenspec change `add-ecosystem-doc-evals` (tasks 2.1–2.5, design D1/D4).\n\n## Why\nBounded pure-Rust module with a crisp TDD shape (harvest tokens → scan docs →\nemit rows) but large breadth: two extractors, a config format, and report\nwiring. Delegation keeps the lead session lean for orchestrating the rest of\nthe epic (phases 3–6 depend on this landing). Independent value: after this\nlands, `just tier0` flags undocumented or unfindable features across the\necosystem the moment docs drift.\n\n## Desired outcome\nNew `src/doc_audit.rs` (Purpose/Responsibilities/Rationale header — e10 Must\ngate) providing:\n1. **Surface extractor** — runs a tool's binary with `--help` (subprocess,\n   in a provisioned fixture sandbox for tests) and harvests a feature-token\n   set: subcommands, long flags, and documented exit codes where `--help`\n   lists them. Token normalization: kebab/snake/spacing variants treated as\n   equivalent (substring-normalized matching per D1).\n2. **Inventory scanner** — scans a repo's docs surfaces (`README.md`,\n   `docs/**`, `llms.txt`, `AGENTS.md` managed blocks) into per-surface\n   feature-token sets.\n3. **Breadcrumb reachability** — a token found in docs but NOT reachable\n   from `llms.txt` or managed-block breadcrumbs → `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`; a\n   token absent from all surfaces → `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`.\n4. **Config** — a checked-in `doc_audit.toml` (tool → repo path, binary\n   name, optional `surface = \"none\"`); `surface: none` tools (e.g. `bd`,\n   `openspec` — not Rust CLIs) skip the binary step and are recorded in\n   provenance, never silently skipped. Absent binaries record provenance\n   `binary_absent` (never silent skip).\n5. **Report wiring** — audit rows flow into the existing report as new\n   check-codes `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED` / `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`;\n   `report_version` stays 1 (additive); `tests/report_aggregation.rs`\n   expectations pass unchanged.\n6. CLI: `evallerina doc-audit` subcommand; wired into `just tier0`.\n\n## Exact files\n- NEW `src/doc_audit.rs` — extractors + scanner + audit rows (MUST carry\n  Purpose header)\n- NEW `doc_audit.toml` — per-tool audit config (all routing.toml tools)\n- `src/lib.rs` — module registration\n- `src/main.rs` — `doc-audit` subcommand + tier-0 wiring\n- `src/report.rs` — accept the two new check-codes (additive only)\n- NEW `tests/doc_audit.rs` — surface + inventory contract tests (failing\n  first); fixture binaries are throwaway shell scripts in a temp dir, NOT\n  real ecosystem binaries\n\n## Red/green sequence\n1. RED: surface test — fixture script prints a `--help` with 2 subcommands +\n   long flags → harvested token set matches, with a kebab/snake pair\n   normalizing to one token. GREEN.\n2. RED: `surface: none` test — tool declared `surface: none` produces no\n   binary probe and records `skip` in provenance. GREEN.\n3. RED: inventory test — fixture repo (temp dir: README + docs/x.md +\n   llms.txt + AGENTS.md managed block) → per-surface token sets. GREEN.\n4. RED: reachability test — token in `docs/x.md` not referenced by\n   `llms.txt`/managed block → `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`; token absent\n   everywhere → `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`; token reachable → no row. GREEN.\n5. RED: `binary_absent` test — configured binary missing → provenance\n   `binary_absent`, loud, not silent. GREEN.\n6. Wire report rows (additive) + CLI + `doc_audit.toml` for the real\n   ecosystem; `just tier0` green. Dogfood check (meter): audit run against\n   evallerina's own surfaces produces a non-empty inventory with zero\n   silent skips.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No routing/filing changes (e4x owns routing audit faults)\n- No new scenario families or tier-2 recordings (vrr/t7n)\n- No report_version bump, no aggregate doc-quality score (anti-goal)\n- No edits to any sibling repo's docs\n\n## Anti-goals\n- Never silently skip a source: every skip is provenance (`skip`,\n  `binary_absent`) — pinned by test\n- No aggregate score field (pinned by test, same discipline as 48g)\n- Token normalization must NOT be tuned to pass evallerina's own docs only\n  (general normalization rules only)\n\n## Commands\n- `cargo test` per red/green step; `just tier0` at end; dogfood:\n  `cargo run -- doc-audit` against evallerina itself → non-empty inventory,\n  zero silent skips\n\n## Follow-up threshold\nIf real-ecosystem audit rows exceed ~40 or the `--help` parsing of any real\ntool resists the extractor (>1h), STOP: record findings as research, ship\nthe mechanism against fixtures, and leave real-tool onboarding notes for\n73q (validation phase). Do not tune normalization to make real rows vanish.\n\n## Verifier evidence contract\nThe verify session's review artifact MUST cite the artifacts it read and\ninclude fresh `cargo test doc_audit` + `just tier0` output before recording\nCONFIRM — otherwise REVIEW_REQUIRED.\n\n## Spawn model\nImplementor: `openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash` (matches PI_PROVIDER default);\ncontext ceiling ≤ 50% of its window, computed at spawn.\n\n[1 more lines in file. Use offset=101 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792527154598},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"6cwVjzuGg","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/.wai/projects/evallerina/research/2026-10-20-evallerina-fok-real-ecosystem-audit-breadth.md","offset":1,"limit":100}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":13712,"output":78,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13790,"cost":{"input":0.0010284,"output":0.0000156,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.001044}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792527154606,"responseId":"gen-1792527154-aqBDliSv48PiuGBiLJpv","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"6cwVjzuGg","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research: evallerina-fok — real-ecosystem doc-audit rows exceed follow-up threshold\n\nDate: 2026-10-20 · Ticket: evallerina-fok · Trigger: brief follow-up threshold\n(\"real-ecosystem audit rows exceed ~40 → STOP, record findings, ship mechanism\nagainst fixtures, leave onboarding notes for 73q\").\n\n## Finding\n\n`cargo run -- doc-audit` against the checked-in `doc_audit.toml` yields **91\naudit rows** across 9 tools (threshold ~40). Breakdown:\n\n- `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`: 77 rows — token documented on some surface but not\n  reachable from llms.txt / AGENTS.md managed-block breadcrumbs. Dominant\n  pattern: most repos document commands/flags in README/docs but have no\n  breadcrumb channel (no llms.txt, or llms.txt that doesn't enumerate the\n  feature). This is the *intended* signal of the gate, not extractor noise.\n- `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`: 14 rows — e.g. `dont color/forget/nopersist/quiet/\n  stats`, `turu quiet/verbose/help`, `specodelic verbose/exit1`, `ah help`,\n  `vampiro completions`, `incitaciones dir`, `pretender help`.\n\nProvenance (16/16 tools accounted, **zero silent skips**): 10 `extracted`,\n4 `binary_absent` (genesis, espectacular, funkalization, dulce-de-leche —\nbinaries not on PATH in this checkout), 2 `skip` (bd, openspec —\n`surface = none` by config).\n\nNo tool's `--help` resisted parsing — the general extractor rules (long flags,\nCommands: sections, exit-code sections) harvested all 10 present binaries\nwithout tool-specific cases. The threshold tripped on breadth (row count), not\nparse resistance.\n\n## D